  "description": "Given an array of events where events[i] = [startDay, endDay], find the maximum number of events that can be attended.",
  "target": null,
  "pseudocode": "1. events.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);\n2. minHeap = [];\n3. d = 1, i = 0, ans = 0;\n4. while(i < n || minHeap.length > 0) {\n5.   if (minHeap.length === 0) d = events[i][0];\n6.   while(i < n && events[i][0] <= d) minHeap.push(events[i++][1]);\n7.   while(minHeap.length > 0 && minHeap[0] < d) minHeap.shift();\n8.   if(minHeap.length > 0) { minHeap.shift(); ans++; d++; }\n9. }",
